# Fixed 2026-11-26, defect 2856 (d-p260-mixedown), lane room-mixedown: a
# header of the program's own declaring a function of the layer's otherwise
# than the layer does, and binding nothing that reaches it, in a program that
# links the layer: one function declared with two types in one program, which
# C leaves undefined, called or not (C11 6.2.7). Told at the group, both
# declarations named with their types.
extern "hero_time.h" layer
    function hero_time_wall_ns() -> i64

extern "fixedbugs-2856-a-layer-function-a-header-declares-otherwise-and-nothing-binds-is-told-at-the-group.h"  #~ ffi_layer_redeclared
    function answer() -> i64

function main()
    print(hero_time_wall_ns() > 0)
    print(answer())
